# Project context

This is a literature review agent for the Open Agent Hackathon 2026 (Track 02: The Agent That Can Explain Why).
The pipeline is described in ARCHITECTURE.md: Planner -> Retriever -> Clusterer -> Connection finder -> Gap finder,
with grading agents after the last three and two human reviews.

# Conventions

- Agents exchange the Pydantic models in `litagent/schemas.py`. Don't pass free text between agents.
- Every connection and gap must carry Evidence (paper id + verbatim quote).
- All LLM calls go through `litagent/integrations/llm.py`.
- Paper data goes through `litagent/integrations/zetaris.py`; agent findings go to the Meterless world model in `litagent/integrations/meterless.py`.
- Tunable numbers live in `litagent/config.py`, not inside agents.
- Log each important decision with `trace.log(...)`, including why.
- Keep the dry-run branch in each agent working; `pytest` runs the pipeline in dry-run mode.
- Never commit keys. Read secrets from `.env` via environment variables.
